    <tags>provisioning, provisioning-handler, l2-controlplane, dataverse, graph, model1-dedicated, tenant-isolation, testing</tags>
    <deps>228</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make H11 leave every Model 1 customer user able to open the customer's Dataverse environment — a redeemed B2B guest in Spaarke's tenant, inside the environment's security group, a Dataverse user holding the Spaarke user role — with access billed pay-as-you-go to that customer's stamp subscription.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (L2 control plane, Microsoft Graph REST, Dataverse Web API, operator skill).</role>

  <goal>
    D2 (owner 2026-09-30): Model 1 customer users are B2B guests in Spaarke's tenant and Spaarke pays.
    Owner decision 2026-10-07 (T232): Spaarke pays through **Power Platform pay-as-you-go** — the operator links each
    customer's Dataverse environment to a billing policy on that customer's stamp subscription; no per-user licences.
    After this task a Model 1 H11 run ends with every listed user able to sign in to the customer's environment, and a
    guest of customer A can never become a user of customer B's environment.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Mapped 2026-10-07 (read-only): H11 invites guests (POST /invitations, mail sent) and waits on the redemption gate
      (externalUserState = Accepted), then completes. Guests get NO licence (assignLicense runs only for NativeAccount,
      and a missing SKU option is skipped silently), NO usageLocation, NO security-group membership, NO Dataverse
      systemuser and NO role — nothing reads InterStepState.ProvisionedUsers. DagAdvancer's comment "its users get the
      solution's roles, imported by H6" is not implemented. Each H11 re-run re-POSTs every invitation, re-sending the mail.
      Model 1 may pick NativeAccount (no tenancyModel × preset rule; the schema's Model 1 example even uses it).
      AccountDomain defaults to spaarke.onmicrosoft.com. The r1 BFF pattern (DemoProvisioningService: group → licence →
      systemuser in a BU → team) is the reference; L2 cannot reference the BFF assembly, so H10's raw-HTTP
      DataverseWebApiAppUserCreator idiom (role lookup in the root BU, systemuserroles_association) is the model to copy.
      Without a security group on the environment, any licensed or PAYG-covered user of Spaarke's tenant — including
      another customer's guest — is admitted on first sign-in; the group is the isolation boundary, not an option.
      Graph roles the Worker needs (User.Invite.All, User.Read.All, GroupMember.ReadWrite.All) are already in the L2
      role catalog (prereqs.yaml "L2 UAMI has Graph app-role grants").
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/UserProvisioning/** (H11 handler, GraphRestB2BInvitationClient, GraphRestB2BConsentVerifier, GraphRestUserProvisioner, UserProvisioningIntake, H11Rejections, options, ProvisionedUserRecord)</file>
      <file>Core/Handlers/DataverseAppUserGraphParity/DataverseWebApiAppUserCreator.cs (raw-HTTP Dataverse idiom + role lookup to copy)</file>
      <file>Core/Models/{IntakeParameterCatalog,InterStepState}.cs; Core/Reconciler/{HandlerRunInputs,DagAdvancer}.cs; Api/Api/RunsEndpoints.cs (ValidateOperatorIntake); Worker/Program.cs (H11 registrations/options)</file>
      <file>scripts/provisioning-prereqs/{intake.schema.json,prereqs.yaml}; .claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md (Step 1 user list, Step 0.5 prereqs)</file>
      <file>docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md (H11 rows, §2 prerequisites); docs/architecture/SPAARKE-ENVIRONMENT-RESOURCE-INVENTORY.md; docs/guides/PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES.md; .claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/{DemoProvisioningService,RegistrationDataverseService}.cs (r1 reference only — do not reference from L2)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
