  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Licensing = pay-as-you-go: no per-user licence assignment for Model 1 guests. Linking the environment to a billing policy on the customer's stamp subscription is an OPERATOR prerequisite (PRQ with a check recipe); L2 creates no billing policy and holds no Power Platform admin role for it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="isolation">Every Model 1 environment has a per-customer environment security group, created by the operator before the environment and named at intake (`environmentSecurityGroupId`, GUID). H11 adds guests ONLY to that group, and refuses (Resumable, naming what it found) a group whose displayName is not `sprk-{customerId}-users`. Nothing is written for a refused run.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D2">Model 1 requires identityPreset B2BGuest (intake 400 otherwise; schema + endpoint parity). Do not break Model 2 / NativeAccount paths (D3).</constraint>
    <constraint source="idempotency">A re-run never re-sends an invitation mail to a user who already exists as a guest (look up by mail first); every step (group membership, systemuser, role) is idempotent and skips what exists.</constraint>
    <constraint source="needed-or-remove">Licence code that only served Model 1 guests is not added. NativeAccount licensing stays as is (Model 2 path) — but a NativeAccount run with no SKU configured must fail visibly, not succeed silently (R7 "validated but not wired").</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests">Real HTTP against hand-written handlers or fakes of the L2 seams; never Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">No live action (invitation, group change, Dataverse write, billing policy) — verify against fakes; live behaviour is a T186 check.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Never run pac with flags to check usage; take any pac syntax for the PRQ recipe from Microsoft documentation (researcher subagent).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Research (researcher subagent, Microsoft Learn): (a) the pac / Power Platform API command that lists a billing policy's linked environments, for the PRQ recipe; (b) whether a Dataverse Web API POST systemuser (azureactivedirectoryobjectid + businessunit) succeeds for a B2B guest who is in the environment security group in a PAYG environment, or whether the BAP/Power Platform "add user to environment" (force sync) call is required; (c) whether Dataverse refuses a systemuser for a user outside the security group. Record findings in notes/t232-guest-access-decisions.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Intake: Model 1 → B2BGuest required; new `environmentSecurityGroupId` (GUID, required for Model 1); catalog + schema (incl. fixing the Model 1 example) + endpoint parity; HandlerRunInputs for H11; tests.</step>
    <step order="3">Invitation: look up an existing guest by mail before inviting; invite (mail sent) only when absent; tests at the HTTP level for the invitation client and the lookup.</step>
    <step order="4">After redemption (existing gate): verify the group's displayName (`sprk-{customerId}-users`), add each guest to it (idempotent: a 400 "already exists" is success), create the Dataverse systemuser per step 1's finding as the Worker identity in the root BU (skip if present), associate the configured role(s) (option, default `Spaarke Basic User`; a missing role → Resumable naming it — the package is T218's), record systemuserid in ProvisionedUsers; tests.</step>
    <step order="5">NativeAccount with no SKU configured → visible failure; remove the "solution's roles, imported by H6" claim or make it true; tests.</step>
    <step order="6">prereqs.yaml (PRQ: environment security group `sprk-{customerId}-users` created and set on the environment before creation; PRQ: environment linked to a PAYG billing policy on the stamp subscription, with recipe); skill (Step 1 asks the group id; Model 1 preset fixed to B2BGuest; Step 0.5 runs both PRQs); guide H11 rows + prerequisites, inventory, PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES, constraints; plan G10 row.</step>
    <step order="7">Verify (ControlPlane tests incl. RunContextContract + schema parity, ArchTests, Worker + Api 0 warnings); Step 9.5; close.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">CreateRun returns 400 for Model 1 with identityPreset NativeAccount, without `environmentSecurityGroupId`, or with a non-GUID value; Model 2 requests are unaffected; schema and endpoint agree (parity tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An H11 re-run for a user who already exists as a guest sends no invitation (asserted at the HTTP level).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A group whose displayName is not `sprk-{customerId}-users` → Resumable refusal naming the group; no membership, systemuser or role write happens.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With the group correct and every guest redeemed: each guest is a group member, has a systemuser and holds the configured role; a second run writes nothing new; ProvisionedUsers carries each systemuserid; the run completes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A configured role that does not exist in the environment → Resumable refusal naming the role.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A NativeAccount run with no SKU configured fails with a named code instead of completing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">prereqs.yaml carries the security-group and PAYG-billing PRQs with recipes; the skill runs them at Step 0.5; no per-user licence assignment exists for B2BGuest.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ControlPlane.Tests and ArchTests pass; Worker/Api build with 0 warnings.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Step 1 finds that adding a guest to a PAYG environment needs a Power Platform admin role for the Worker identity (force sync) — ask the owner before granting or designing around it.</trigger>
    <trigger>Step 1 finds pay-as-you-go cannot cover B2B guests, or needs a licence after all.</trigger>
    <trigger>A live action would be required to verify — ask the owner first.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <notes>
    COMPLETED 2026-10-07 (SESSION 41). Commits c5df5f07c (code), tests, 466e75e75 (docs/PRQs), 07a92eca3 (round 1),
    79ca02b3c (round 2), master merge 512cd2304 (+ 7f908c2dc merge semantic fix), 67a7bf446 (round 3, owner-approved),
    plus this close. Decisions D1–D12 + known limits K1–K10: notes/t232-guest-access-decisions.md.
    - Owner 2026-10-07: Spaarke pays guest access PAY-AS-YOU-GO on the customer's stamp subscription (no per-user
      licences); the per-app meter (~$10 per active user per app per month) ACCEPTED.
    - Intake: Model1 → B2BGuest only (userprov-model1-requires-b2b-guest); B2BGuest needs environmentSecurityGroupId
      (canonical GUID; userprov-missing/invalid-security-group-id); a repeated guest email refused. Schema + catalog +
      endpoint + HandlerRunInputs (+ Output DataverseEnvUrl) in parity.
    - H11 B2BGuest: before inviting anyone — H5's DataverseEnvUrl, the group named sprk-{customerId}-users and
      security-enabled (userprov-security-group-rejected), restrictguestuseraccess off (userprov-guest-access-restricted),
      the guest roles resolved once in the root BU (reusing H8's IDataverseRootBusinessUnitReader; missing → named,
      ambiguous → refused). An existing guest is reused — no second invitation email; a Member address refused. After
      every guest redeems: group membership (idempotent), systemuser via the azureactivedirectoryobjectid alternate key
      (Dataverse adds a group member on demand — Microsoft's app-only path; no Power Platform admin role), role
      association if not held; systemuserid in ProvisionedUsers. NativeAccount with no licence SKU creates nobody.
      Every collaborator timeout is a named Resumable failure.
    - New seams: IEnvironmentSecurityGroupClient (Graph), IDataverseGuestUserWriter (Web API); options validated at start
      (GuestSecurityRoleNames default applied after binding).
    - PRQ-C-10 (group, and that it is SET ON the environment — operator-only, checked by the skill through the Power
      Platform admin API), PRQ-C-11 (PAYG billing policy on the stamp subscription), PRQ-C-12 (guest access) — prereqs
      manifest v9; skill Step 1e-bis checks all three as the operator (deviation D9: not Step 0.5 — once-per-customer
      checks are deferred there by design). Guide, inventory, PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES v7, constraints section, CHANGELOG.
    - Step 9.5: code-review (4 W, 12 S) + adr-check (1 V ADR-044, 10 W) → round 1; verifier → 8 new (round 2); final
      verifier → 1 Critical (skill az.cmd broke on ')' in RetrieveCurrentOrganization — every Model 1 run would hard-stop)
      escalated under the old 2-round cap; owner approved the fix and withdrew the cap repo-wide (merged from master) →
      round 3; fix-diff re-verification: all verified, K-notes only.
    - Tests: ControlPlane 2275/0 (1 skip); ArchTests 836/836; BFF full (post-merge): see the close commit. Worker + Api
      0 warnings. No BFF code changed by T232.
    - T186 live checks: on-demand add of an unlicensed guest under PAYG (alternate key); the BAP / RetrieveCurrentOrganization
      response shapes the skill reads (K6); pac licensing output shape (K3 — anchor the Enabled match then).
  </notes>
</task>
